From f02253ac48552ec98926aed2dbcc0091e2824256 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:21:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] board: zte: add the web bootloader rescue (e2631rescue)

Add e2631rescue, a console command that turns lan1 into a self-contained
recovery network without rebooting and without touching flash by itself:

  - DHCP: 192.168.1.1/24, pool from 192.168.1.100;
  - HTTP: GET / serves the gzip rescue page generated at build time from
    uboot-port/failsafe/e2631-failsafe.html, GET /status reports the
    key=value progress snapshot, and POST /flash?mode=validate|write
    accepts one raw 655360-byte mtd0 image;
  - the body is staged at 0x46000000 (1 MiB, clear of the kernel load
    area, the uImage staging area and the network DMA arena) and checked
    before any erase: exact size, vendor header magic, payload length
    window, 0xff padding, "U-Boot 20" banner and the SHA-256 sent in
    X-E2631-SHA256. A write also needs X-E2631-Confirm: write; a missing
    or mismatched digest refuses with an error and no erase;
  - an accepted write runs the e2631flash five-step sequence through the
    shared job API, only inside mtd0 0x20000..0xA0000. secondboot, the
    environment block and the reserved tail are never touched;
  - every stage is published on /status; a failure is reported both on the
    page and on the console. Nothing reboots automatically, and normal
    boot never starts the network.

The board Makefile links the generated page asset and the defconfig
enables CONFIG_MTK_TCP, CONFIG_MTK_DHCPD and CONFIG_SHA256. The page
asset step already runs in the build workflow before the compile.

The rescue write covers the whole U-Boot area: source = image start,
offset 0x20000, length 0xA0000, ending at the environment block. The
compile-time asserts tie that end to CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
